# tests/ is LF by convention (enforced by tests/test_line_endings.py).
#
# Git for Windows checks files out with core.autocrlf=true by default, which
# turned every tests/*.py into CRLF on the windows-latest runner and broke that
# gate.  Pin the working-tree format so the convention does not depend on each
# developer's git config.
#
# Deliberately NOT declared here: superfreetts_addon/**, which is stored as
# CRLF in the index.  A text/eol=crlf rule for it would renormalise 651 tracked
# blobs on the next commit and rewrite every line of the add-on source.
tests/** text eol=lf
